friendly.content:
{{also|Friendly}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈfɹɛnd.li/|/ˈfɹɛn.li/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-friendly.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛndli|ɛnli|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|frendly}}, {{m|enm|freendly}}, {{m|enm|frendely}}, {{m|enm|frendlich}}, from {{inh|en|ang|frēondlīċ}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*frijōndlīkaz}}, equivalent to {{af|en|friend|-ly|id2=adjectival}}. Cognate with {{cog|stq|früntelk}}, {{m|stq|fjuntelk|t=friendly}}, {{cog|fy|freonlik|t=friendly}}, {{cog|nl|vriendelijk|t=friendly}}, {{cog|nds-de|fründelk}}, {{m|nds-de|frünnelk|t=friendly}}, {{cog|de|freundlich|t=friendly}}. {{doublet|en|friendlike}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|er,more}}

# Generally [[warm]], [[approachable]] and [[easy]] to [[relate]] with in [[character]].
#: {{syn|en|[[chummy]] (informal)}}
#: {{ux|en|Your cat seems very '''friendly'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Marshall Squire's Daughter|A Court Ball|9|They stayed together during three dances, went out on to the terrace, explored wherever they were permitted to explore, paid two visits to the buffet, and enjoyed themselves much in the same way as if they had been school-children surreptitiously breaking loose from an assembly of grown-ups. The boy became volubly '''friendly''' and bubbling over with unexpected humour and high spirits.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Brothers on the Bashkaus: A Siberian Paddling Adventure|page=36|author=Eugene Buchanan|year=2007|passage=Our '''friendliest''' carmates are a family from Armenia taking a vacation from the Georgian war.}}
# {{U|inviting}}, [[characteristic]] of [[friendliness]].
#: {{syn|en|familiar}}
#: {{ux|en|He gave a '''friendly''' smile.}}
# Having an easy or accepting relationship with something.
#: {{ux|en|a user-'''friendly''' software program}}
#: {{ux|en|a dog-'''friendly''' café}}
#: {{ux|en|the use of '''[[environmentally friendly]]''' packaging}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1956|month=January|author='Mercury'|title=The Railways of North-East Switzerland|journal=Railway Magazine|page=23|text=The inter-working of the Bodensee-Toggenburg, Swiss South-Eastern and Swiss Federal Railways is of a '''most friendly''' kind.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2016-10-22|author=Rami G Khouri|title=Lebanese oligarchy preserves its interests once again
|work=w:Aljazeera|url=http://www.aljazeera.com/indepth/opinion/2016/10/lebanese-oligarchy-preserves-interests-161021075017806.html|passage=Hariri even nominated Hezbollah-'''friendly''' Sleiman Frangieh for the presidency, which by tradition is held by a Maronite Christian; but Hezbollah and Aoun held out, insisting that Aoun would be president or there would be no president at all.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20191229223943/https://www.aljazeera.com/indepth/opinion/2016/10/lebanese-oligarchy-preserves-interests-161021075017806.html|archivedate=29 December 2019}}
#* {{quote-journal|1=en|author=Krisztian Sandor|title=Binance's BNB Hits Fresh Record, Breaks Out of 3-Year Range as Altcoin Rotation Accelerates|magazine=w:CoinDesk|url=https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2024/12/04/binance-s-bnb-hits-fresh-record-breaks-out-of-3-year-range-as-altcoin-rotation-accelerates|date=2024-12-04|passage=Older cryptocurrencies with regulatory overhang including Ripple's XRP and TRX were among the biggest gainers over the past month as Donald Trump's election victory promises a '''friendlier''' regulatory environment towards digital assets.|accessdate=7 December 2024|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20241208054713/https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2024/12/04/binance-s-bnb-hits-fresh-record-breaks-out-of-3-year-range-as-altcoin-rotation-accelerates|archivedate=8 December 2024}}
# {{lb|en|in compounds}} [[compatible|Compatible with]], or not damaging to (the compounded noun).
#: {{ux|en|The cobbled streets aren't very bike-'''friendly'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|Organic farms only use soil-'''friendly''' fertilisers.}}
#: {{ux|en|Our sandwiches are made with dolphin-'''friendly''' tuna.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=Tony Pinchuck; Barbara McCrea; Donald Reid; Ross Velton|title=The Rough Guide to South Africa|edition=6th|location=London|publisher=w:Rough Guides|isbn=978-1-84836-433-2|page=147–148|passage=An offbeat pizza restaurant, which also serves pasta and salads, and bills itself as low-fat and heart-'''friendly'''. Has over forty different designer pizza toppings, such as smoked salmon, sour cream and caviar.}}
# Without any [[hostility]].
#: {{ux|en|a '''friendly''' competition}}
#: {{ux|en|a '''friendly''' power or state}}
#* {{RQ:Macaulay History of England|chapter=2|passage=in '''friendly''' relations with his moderate opponents}}
# Promoting the good of any person; favourable; propitious.
#: {{ux|en|a '''friendly''' breeze or gale}}
#* {{RQ:Addison Cato|scene=iv|page=10|passage=Coarſe are his Meals, the Fortune of the Chaſe, / Amidſt the running Stream he ſlakes his Thirſt, / Toil's all the Day, and at th' approach of Night / On the firſt '''friendly''' Bank he throws him down, / Or reſts his Head upon a Rock 'till Morn: {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|usually|military}} Of or pertaining to [[friendlies]] (''friendly'' noun sense 2, below). Also applied to other bipolar confrontations, such as team sports.
#: {{ux|en|The soldier was killed by [['''friendly''' fire]].}}
# {{lb|en|number theory}} Being or relating to two or more [[natural number]]s with a common [[abundancy]].
#: {{ux|en|'''friendly'''}}
#: {{ux|en|'''friendly''' pairs}}
#: {{ux|en|'''friendly''' n-tuples}}

