===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|-|s}}

# {{senseid|en|Q2}}{{C|en|Planets of the Solar System}}The [[third]] [[planet]] of the [[Solar System]]; the [[world]] upon which [[human]]s [[live]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Macbeth|I|iii|page=132|passage=What are theſe, / So wither’d, and ſo wilde in their attyre. / That looke not like th’Inhabitants o’th’'''Earth''', / And yet are on’t?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Ken Adams|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=RU5wbv0IWtkC&pg=PA85&dq=%22many+Earths%22&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwjc16-glfbSAhUqsFQKHes9BpE4HhDoAQgrMAM#v=onepage&q=%22many%20Earths%22&f=false|title=Earth 2... It's Where You Go When You Die|passage=It's my theory that we'll keep being reborn on as many '''Earths''' as it takes until every person gets it exactly right from the moment they are born until the moment they die.}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|author=Ian Sample|title=Earth weighs in at six ronnagrams as new prefixes picked for big and small|url=https://www.theguardian.com/science/2022/nov/18/earth-six-ronnagrams-new-prefixes-big-and-small|date=2022-11-18|passage=The arrival of the new prefixes means the '''Earth''' can now be said to weigh six ronnagrams, and Jupiter about two quettagrams.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261017221703/https://www.theguardian.com/science/2022/nov/18/earth-six-ronnagrams-new-prefixes-big-and-small|archivedate=17 October 2026}}
#* {{see more citations|en}}
# The [[personification]] of the Earth or [[earth]], {{lb|en|chiefly}} as a [[fertile]] [[woman]] or {{lb|en|religion}} [[goddess]].

====Usage notes====
* {{m|en|Earth}} may be used with or without {{m|en|the}}. Contrast other planets (e.g. {{m|en|Mars}}, {{m|en|Jupiter}}) which never take an article, and certain other celestial bodies (e.g. {{m|en|Sun}}, {{m|en|Moon}}) which always do.

The capitalized form usually occurs when it is contrasted with the names of other celestial bodies or realms:
: {{ux|en|From the '''Earth''' to the Moon}}
: {{ux|en|What is the distance between '''Earth''' and Mars?}}

