===Preposition===
{{ga-prep|d|h}}

# [[to]] (with places), [[till]], [[until]]
#: {{uxi|ga|dul '''go''' Meiriceá|to go to America}}
#: {{uxi|ga|Fáilte '''go''' hÉirinn|Welcome to Ireland}}
#: {{uxi|ga|'''go''' leor|enough, plenty, galore|lit=until plenty}}
#: {{uxi|ga|'''go''' fóill|still, yet, till later, in a while, later on}}

====Usage notes====
* In the meaning {{m-g|to}}, used with place names that do not start with the definite article. Place names that do start with the definite article use {{m|ga|go dtí}} instead. In a few fixed phrases, the archaic form {{m|ga|gos}} is used.
* The inflected forms that originally belonged to this preposition (that is, the prepositional pronouns meaning {{m-g|to me}} etc.) have been reanalyzed as the inflected forms of {{m|ga|chuig}}.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|ga|go dtí}}

===Particle===
{{head|ga|particles}} {{q|triggers {{ga-mut-link|h}}}}

# {{n-g|used to make temporary state [[adverb]]s}}
#: {{ux|inline=1|ga|D’ith sé '''go''' maith.|He ate well.}}
#: {{ux|inline=1|ga|Shiúlaíodar '''go''' mall.|They walked slowly.}}
#: {{ux|inline=1|ga|'''go''' feargach|angrily}}
# {{n-g|used to make [[predicative]] [[adjective]]s expressing an [[opinion]] or [[value judgment]]}}
#: {{ux|inline=1|ga|Tá an t-anraith seo '''go''' maith.|This soup is good.}}
#: {{ux|inline=1|ga|Bhí a mac '''go''' hálainn.|Her son was beautiful.}}
#: {{ux|inline=1|ga|Ní raibh an scannán '''go''' huafásach.|The film wasn't awful.}}

====Usage notes====
Only used with predicate adjectives expressing a value judgment like "good/bad", "beautiful/ugly" etc. Other predicate adjectives do not take a particle:
: {{ux|inline=1|ga|Tá an t-anraith seo te.|This soup is hot.}}
: {{ux|inline=1|ga|Bhí a mac ard.|Her son was tall.}}
: {{ux|inline=1|ga|Ní raibh an film fada.|The film wasn't long.}}

