===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# Happening [[quickly]] and with little or no [[warning]]; in a [[sudden]] manner.
#: {{synonyms|en|all of a sudden}}
#: {{antonyms|en|unsuddenly}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Suddenly''', the heavens opened and we all got drenched.}}
#: {{ux|en|They've '''suddenly''' decided to sell the house.}}
#* {{RQ:Grafton Chronicle|volume=II|chapter=[[w:Henry V of England|Henrye the Fift]]|page=464|passage=The king before he would take his voyage, sent the [[w:John Holland, 2nd Duke of Exeter|Erle of Huntyngdon]] to ſerche and ſcowre the Seas, leaſt any Frenchmen lyeng in wayte for him might attrap him '''sodeinly''', or he had any knowledge of their ſetting forward.}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Wayne Darsh|title=A child of war, with a sense of purpose|url=https://www.cnn.com/2013/09/08/us/alison-spann-daughter-of-war|date=2013-09-08|passage=Shannon Spann had an infant, Jake, to care for and two stepdaughters to '''suddenly''' raise by herself.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250715082148/https://edition.cnn.com/2013/09/08/us/alison-spann-daughter-of-war/}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Oliver Brown|title=Oscar Pistorius jailed for five years – sport afforded no protection against his tragic fallibilities: Bladerunner's punishment for killing Reeva Steenkamp is but a frippery when set against the burden that her bereft parents, June and Barry, must carry &#91;print version: No room for sentimentality in this tragedy, 13 September 2014, p.&nbsp;S22&#93;|url=http://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/worldnews/oscar-pistorius/11089621/Oscar-Pistorius-jailed-for-five-years-sport-afforded-no-protection-against-his-tragic-fallibilities.html|work={{w|The Daily Telegraph}} (Sport)|date=21 October 2014|passage=But ever since the concept of "hamartia" recurred through {{w|Aristotle}}'s ''[[w:Poetics (Aristotle)|Poetics]]'', in an attempt to describe man's ingrained iniquity, our impulse has been to identify a telling defect in those brought '''suddenly''' and dramatically low.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250715081422/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/worldnews/oscar-pistorius/11089621/Oscar-Pistorius-jailed-for-five-years-sport-afforded-no-protection-against-his-tragic-fallibilities.html|archivedate=15 July 2025}}

