# {{senseid|en|spend the springtime}}{{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[spend]] the [[springtime]] [[somewhere]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Northern Germany. A Sketch.|journal=[[w:Fraser's Magazine|Fraser’s Magazine for Town and Country]]|volume=XI|issue=LXV|month=May|year=1835|page=507|passage=True it is that, owing to the migratory propensities of our countrymen, every third man has wintered at Naples, '''springed''' at Vienna, summered in Switzerland, and autumned on the banks of the Lago Maggiore;}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=William C[yrus] Sprague|title=Tad, the Story of a Boy who Had No Chance|year=1912|page=2|passage=If Tad’s father and Tad had wintered, '''springed''', summered, and autumned together for an hundred years instead of fifteen they could{{...}}}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Mortimer Jones|title=Lines of No Importance|journal=The Alphi Phi Quarterly|year=1937|page=29|passage=They wintered in a warm place <br> And summered in a cold, <br> But where they '''springed''' and autumned <br> I never have been told.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=Chambers’s Journal|year=1950|page=269|passage=She '''springed''' in London, summered in Stockholm, autumned at Vichy, and wintered at Monte Carlo.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Tim Pratt|chapter=The Third-Quarter King|editors=w:Jonathan Strahan; Jeremy G Byrne|title=w:Eidolon I|year=2006|page=2|isbn=9780809562343|passage=In recent years his friend the fourth-quarter king summered, autumned, and '''springed''' in nearby Southern California, which was how they stayed so easily in touch.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Larry Stettner; Bill Morrison|title=Cooking for the Common Good: The Birth of a Natural Foods Soup Kitchen|location=Berkeley, Calif.|publisher=w:North Atlantic Books|year=2010|page=84|isbn=978-1-55643-957-5|passage=Larry and Bill had planned to hold a white-linen “fancy” fund-raiser dinner in late June or early July, which would bring out the moneyed crowd who “summered” on the Island. If you summer or winter somewhere you are affluent, Larry knew. (Funny, though, he had never heard of anyone who “autumned” in Vermont or who was “'''springing'''” in Colorado.)}}

