#* {{RQ:Milton Hirelings|pages=57–58|pageref=58|passage=[H]e, a lollard indeed over his elbovv-cuſhion, in almoſt the '''ſeaventh''' part of 40. or 50. years teaches them ſcarce half the principles of religion; and his ſheep oft-times ſit the vvhile to as little purpoſe of benifiting as the ſheep in thir pues at ''Smithfield''; {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1976|author={{w|Lilian Hamilton Jeffery|L{{quote-gloss|ilian}} H{{quote-gloss|amilton}} Jeffery}}|chapter=Kylon and Drakon|title=Archaic Greece: The City-States, c. 700-500 {{smallcaps|b.c.}}|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher={{w|St. Martin's Press|St. Martin’s Press}}|section=section II (Central and Northern Greece), subsection 7 (Athens and Attica)|page=86|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/archaicgreece0000unse/page/86/mode/1up|lccn=75-10758|oclc=2168157|passage=[T]he law codes drafted in Athens in the late '''seventh''' and early sixth centuries were the work of individuals, Drakon and then Solon.}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|author=Jack Schofield|title=How can I tell if a PC processor is any good?|url=https://www.theguardian.com/technology/askjack/2017/jan/19/how-can-i-tell-if-a-pc-processor-is-any-good|date=2017-01-19|passage=Intel usually brings out a new generation of processors every 12-18 months, and the Core range is now in its '''seventh''' generation.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261018140104/https://www.theguardian.com/technology/askjack/2017/jan/19/how-can-i-tell-if-a-pc-processor-is-any-good|archivedate=18 October 2026}}
#* {{quote-web|1=en|title=2023 Laws of Chess|url=https://rcc.fide.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/20230101Laws-of-Chess.pdf|year=2022|page=21|work=w:FIDE|passage=Consequently, in the initial position the white pieces and pawns are placed on the first and second ranks; the black pieces and pawns on the eighth and '''seventh''' ranks.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250316122506/https://rcc.fide.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/20230101Laws-of-Chess.pdf|archivedate=16 March 2025|accessdate=19 October 2025}}

