#* {{quote-book|en|author=John L. Bullion|chapter=Jokes|title=In the Boat with [[w:Lyndon B. Johnson|LBJ]]|location=Plano, Tex.|publisher=Republic of Texas Press|year=2001|page=294|isbn=978-1-55622-880-3|passage=Whenever I started drinking again after abstaining for any period of time, it usually was an effort to relieve stress and to "'''happy''' up."}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Wayne Kaatz|chapter=11|title=Stuck on Earth|location=Bloomington, Ind.|publisher=[[w:Simon & Schuster|Archway Publishing]]|date=18 July 2016|isbn=978-1-4808-3280-0|passage=[H]e smiled {{...}} then asked my name. He checked it against his clipboard then sadly shook his head as if he'd been rejected himself. Told him I was looking for employment and he '''happied''' up again, able to help by directing me to apply at the front office, that the doors were on the Gower Street side.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|informal}} ''Often followed by'' '''{{l|en|up}}''': to [[make]] happy; to [[brighten]], to [[cheer#Verb|cheer]], to [[enliven]].
#: {{syn|en|bright|cheer up|happify|perk up|Thesaurus:gladden}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Mireille Juchau|chapter=Sanctuary|title=Burning In|location=Artarmon, N.S.W.|publisher={{w|Giramondo Publishing}} for the Writing & Society Research Group, {{w|University of Western Sydney}}|year=2007|page=201|isbn=978-1-920882-27-3|passage=People really didn't want their Party Motivators in their photos, anonymous dancers, '''happying''' up the place. It spooked them.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Nickolas Martin|title=Ego Therapy: A Method for Healing Your Whole Self|location=Bloomington, Ind.|publisher=Balboa Press, {{w|Hay House}}|date=26 October 2015|isbn=978-1-5043-4282-7|passage={{...}} [[w:William Glasser|[William] Glasser]] would probably say that happy people are "'''happying'''" themselves by choosing behaviors that help them to feel happy (working at their relationships, engaging in productive work activities, participating in desired recreational activities, etc.).}}

