# {{lb|en|historical}} A type of [[ale]] traditionally brewed in October. {{defdate|from 18th c.}}
#* {{RQ:Addison Drummer|page=46|passage=Sir, if I vvas vvorthy to adviſe you, I vvou'd have a Bottle of good '''''October''''' by me. Shall I ſet a Cup of old Stingo at your Elbovv?}}
#* {{RQ:Smollett Peregrine Pickle|volume=IV|114|passage=[T]he gate of a large ''chateau'', of a most noble and venerable appearance {{...}} induced them to alight and view the apartments, contrary to their first intention of drinking a glass of his '''October''' at the door.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1898|author=Stanley John Weyman|chapter=III. Tutor and Pupils|title=The Castle Inn|passage=Sir George, borne along in his chair, peered up at this well-known window--well-known, since in the Oxford of 1767 a man's rooms were furnished if he had tables and chairs, store of beef and '''October''', an apple-pie and Common Room port—and seeing the casement brilliantly lighted, smiled a trifle contemptuously.}}

