#* {{RQ:ang:Thorpe Chronicle|entry=741|page=78|text=<small>An. DCCXLI</small> Hēr Æþelheard cing forðferde, ⁊ feng Cūþrēd tō Westseaxna rīċe, ⁊ heold XXVI '''wintra''', ⁊ heardlīċe hē ġewann wiþ Æþelwald cing. ⁊ Cūþbriht wæs tō arċebisċeope ġehālgod, ⁊ Dunn bisċeop tō Hrofesċeastre.|t=<small>Year 741</small> In this year King Aethelhard died, and Cuthred ascended to the West Saxon throne. He held it for 26 '''years''', and fought bravely against King Aethelwald. And Cuthbright was ordained archbishop, and Dunn ordained bishop of Rochester.}}

