===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To determine the weight of an object.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} Often with "out", to [[measure]] a [[certain]] [[amount]] of [[something]] by its [[weight]], e.g. for sale.
#: {{ux|en|He '''weighed''' out two kilos of oranges for a client.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|figuratively}} To [[determine]] the [[intrinsic]] [[value]] or [[merit]] of an object, to [[evaluate]].
#: {{syn|en|assess|price|value|Thesaurus:appraise}}
#: {{ux|en|You have been '''weighed''' in the balance and found wanting.}}
#: {{ux|en|He took a long time '''weighing''' his options.}}
