===Etymology===
{{ety|en|tree=1|:inh|enm:wrong}}
From {{inh|en|enm|wrong}}, from {{inh|en|ang|wrang|id=wrong|t=wrong, twisted, uneven}}, from {{der|en|non|rangr}}, {{m|non|vrangr|t=crooked, wrong}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*wrangaz|t=crooked, twisted, turned awry}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*werḱ-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*wrengʰ-|t=to twist, weave, tie together}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*wer-|t=to turn, bend}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|wrang|t=wrong}}, {{cog|da|vrang|t=wrong, crooked}}, {{cog|sv|vrång|t=perverse, distorted}}, {{cog|is|rangur|t=wrong}}, {{cog|nn|rang|t=wrong}}, {{cog|nl|wrang|t=bitter, sour}} and the first element in the mythic {{cog|ofs|-}} city of {{m|ofs|Rungholt|t=crooked wood}}. More at {{m|en|wring}}.

