==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*kap-|id=seize}}
From {{inh|en|enm|hevy}}, {{m|enm|heviȝ}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hefiġ}}, {{m|ang|hefeġ}}, {{m|ang|hæfiġ|t=heavy; important, grave, severe, serious; oppressive, grievous; slow, dull}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*habīg|t=heavy, hefty, weighty}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*habīgaz|t=heavy, hefty, weighty}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*kap-|id=seize|t=to take, grasp, hold}}. Equivalent to {{suf|en|heave|-y}}. Related to {{m|en|have}}.

Cognate with {{cog|sco|hevy}}, {{m|sco|havy}}, {{m|sco|heavy|t=heavy}}, {{cog|stq|heeuwich}}, {{m|stq|häwich|t=violent, angry}}, {{cog|fy|hevich|t=violent}}, {{cog|nl|hevig|t=violent, severe, intense, acute}}, {{cog|nds-de|hevig|t=violent, fierce, intense, angry}}, {{cog|de|hebig}} (compare {{m|de|heftig|t=fierce, severe, intense, violent, heavy}}), {{cog|is|höfugur|t=heavy, weighty, important}}.

Compare typologically {{ncog|ru|взять,объёмный,ёмкий|ng=akin to {{m|ru|име́ть}}}}, and {{ncog|la|capāx|t=large, wide, roomy, spacious, capacious, capable, apt}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{enPR|hevʹi}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈhɛv.i/|a=RP,GA}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈhev.i/|a=AU,NZ}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-heavy.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|EN-AU ck1 heavy.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛvi|s=2}}

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|er}}
[[File:2008-03-11 Men lifting a dresser.jpg|thumb|250px|right|Four men lifting a '''heavy''' sideboard.]]

# {{lb|en|of any physical thing}} Having great [[weight]].
#: {{ux|en|Can you help me carry this? It's really '''heavy'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|Use the scales to measure how '''heavy''' it is.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=2|passage=Sunning himself on the board steps, I saw for the first time Mr. Farquhar Fenelon Cooke.{{...}}A silver snaffle on a '''heavy''' leather watch guard which connected the pockets of his corduroy waistcoat, together with a huge gold stirrup in his Ascot tie, sufficiently proclaimed his tastes.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2002|author=Eva Brann|title=Homeric Moments|page=48
|passage=But now, ten years later, after his recent shipwreck, he cannot compete as a runner, though he can outthrow the slighter Phaeacians with the '''heaviest''' discus.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2015-05-18|author=Angus Chen|journal=[https://www.npr.org/sections/thesalt/2015/05/18/403364557/how-we-store-food-at-home-could-be-linked-to-how-much-we-eat How We Store Food At Home Could Be Linked To How Much We Eat]|passage=In other research, scientists have found that people who kept cereal out in the open were often about 20 pounds '''heavier''' than people who kept cereal behind closed doors.}}
## {{lb|en|of a person}} [[heavyset#Adjective|Heavyset]]: [[overweight#Adjective|overweight]].
##: {{ux|en|When he was a child he was rather '''heavy''', but today he is impressively fit.}}
# {{lb|en|of a topic}} {{U|serious}}, [[somber]].
#* {{quote-web|en|author=w:Howard Tayler|work=w:Schlock Mercenary|date=8 January 2020|url=https://www.schlockmercenary.com/2020-01-08|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250213033908/https://www.schlockmercenary.com/2020-01-08|archivedate=13 February 2025|accessdate=12 February 2025|text="We're still in an existential-stakes war with the Pa'anuri, and possibly with our own destructive tendencies."  ''<beat panel>''  "Sorry.  That was pretty '''heavy''' for someone who just woke up."  "Oh, I'm fine.  Waking up alive has ALWAYS meant spending the day trying not to be dead."}}
# Not easy to [[bear]]; [[burdensome]]; [[oppressive]].
#: {{ux|en|'''heavy''' yokes, expenses, undertakings, trials, news, etc.}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|1 Samuel|5|6|passage=The hand of the Lord was '''heavy''' upon them of Ashdod.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Henry 5|IV|i|passage=The king himself hath a '''heavy''' reckoning to make.}}
#* {{RQ:Wordsworth The Excursion|passage=Sent hither by my Husband to impart the '''heavy''' news.}}
# {{lb|en|British|slang|dated}} [[good|Good]].
#: {{ux|en|This film is '''heavy'''.}}
# {{lb|en|dated|late 1960s|1970s|US}} [[profound|Profound]].
#: {{ux|en|The Moody Blues are, like, '''heavy'''.}}
# {{lb|en|of a rate of flow}} [[high|High]], [[great]].
#* '''1998''', Stanley George Clayton, "[https://www.britannica.com/science/menstruation "Menstruation"] in ''Encyclopedia Britannica''
#*: The ovarian response to gonadotropic hormones may be erratic at first, so that irregular or '''heavy''' bleeding sometimes occurs
# {{lb|en|slang}} [[armed|Armed]].
#: {{ux|en|Come '''heavy''', or not at all.}}
# {{lb|en|of music}} Loud, distorted, or intense.
#: {{ux|en|Metal is '''heavier''' than rock.}}
# {{lb|en|of weather}} [[hot|Hot]] and [[humid]].
# Doing the [[specified]] activity more [[intensely]] than most other people.
#: {{ux|en|This car is too '''heavy''' on gas.}} 
#: {{ux|en|He was a '''heavy''' sleeper, a '''heavy''' eater and a '''heavy''' smoker – certainly not an ideal husband.}}
#* {{RQ:Thackeray Pendennis||passage=He was described in the theatrical prints as the “veteran Blenkinsop”—“the useful Blenkinsop”—“that old favourite of the public, Blenkinsop”—those parts in the drama, which are called the '''heavy''' fathers, were usually assigned to this veteran, who, indeed, acted the '''heavy''' father in public, as in private life.|29}}
# {{lb|en|of the eyes}} With [[eyelid]]s difficult to keep open due to [[tiredness]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=Dec 2021|journal= The Road Ahead|location=Brisbane|page=11|column=3|text=Watch for the signs of fatigue, including yawning, blinking and '''heavy''' eyes.}}
# {{lb|en|of food}} High in [[fat]] or [[protein]]; [[difficult]] to [[digest]].
#: {{ux|en|Cheese-stuffed sausage is too '''heavy''' to eat before exercising.}}
# Of great [[force]], [[power]], or [[intensity]]; [[deep]] or [[intense]].
#: {{ux|en|it was a '''heavy''' storm;&nbsp; a '''heavy''' slumber in bed;&nbsp; a '''heavy''' punch}}
#* {{RQ:Burroughs Land That Time Forgot||IV|passage=The surf was not '''heavy''', and there was no undertow, so we made shore easily, effecting an equally easy landing.}}
#* {{RQ:Economist|date=2013-07-20|volume=408|issue=8845| title=Out of the gloom|url=http://www.economist.com/news/http://www.economist.com/news/asia/21582043-villagers-enjoy-sunlight-after-dark-out-gloom| passage=[Rural solar plant] schemes are of little help to industry or other '''heavy''' users of electricity. Nor is solar power yet as cheap as the grid. For all that, the rapid arrival of electric light to Indian villages is long overdue. When the national grid suffers its next huge outage, as it did in July 2012 when hundreds of millions were left in the dark, look for specks of light in the villages.}}
# [[laden|Laden]] with that which is [[weighty]]; [[encumbered]]; [[burdened]]; [[bowed down]], either with an actual [[burden]], or with [[grief]], [[pain]], [[disappointment]], etc.
#: {{ux|en|his eyes were '''heavy''' with sleep;&nbsp; she was '''heavy''' [[with child]]}}
#* {{RQ:Homer Chapman Odysseys|year=1857|passage=The '''heavy''' [sorrowing] nobles all in council were.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Merchant of Venice|V|i|passage=A light wife doth make a '''heavy''' husband.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1613|author=w:William Browne|title=Britannia's Pastorals
|passage=Seating himselfe within a darkesome cave, / (Such places '''heavy''' Saturnists doe crave,) / Where yet the gladsome day was never seene {{...}}}}
# [[slow|Slow]]; [[sluggish]]; [[inactive]]; or [[lifeless]], [[dull]], [[inanimate]], [[stupid]].
#: {{ux|en|a '''heavy''' gait, looks, manners, style, etc.}}
#: {{ux|en|a '''heavy''' writer or book}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Midsummer|V|i|passage=whilst the '''heavy''' ploughman snores}}
#* {{RQ:Dryden Fables|Cymon and Iphigenia
|passage=a '''heavy''', dull, degenerate mind}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Isaiah|59|1|passage=Neither [is] his ear '''heavy''', that it cannot hear.}}
# Impeding motion; [[cloggy]]; [[clayey]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1861|title=Mountain Charley|author=E. J. Guerin|page=37|text=The next day we only made some eight miles, as the road was '''heavy''' beyond all belief. It lay through a desert region of country which was ancle-deep {{sic}} in soda and alkali dust.}}
#: ''a '''heavy''' road; a '''heavy''' soil''
# Not [[raised]] or [[leavened]].
#: {{ux|en|'''heavy''' bread}}
# {{lb|en|of [[wine]]s or [[spirit]]s}} Having much [[body]] or [[strength]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[with child|With child]]; [[pregnant]].
# {{lb|en|physics}} Containing one or more [[isotope]]s that are heavier than the normal one.
#: {{ux|en|[[heavy water|'''heavy''' water]]}}
# {{lb|en|petroleum}} Of [[petroleum]], having high [[viscosity]].
# {{lb|en|finance}} Of a [[market]]: in which the [[price]] of [[share]]s is declining.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1819|journal=The Scots Magazine|volume=83-84|page=577
|passage=The very low prices of brandy, and the continuance of a '''heavy''' market for such a length of time, have begun to attract buyers; {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1922|title=The Investor's Monthly Manual: A Newspaper for Investors|page=626
|passage=The oil market is '''heavy''', each day bringing along further supplies of shares from people who have not tired of the long-continued decline in the market.}}
