[[File:Young Woman Wearing U.S. Army T-shirt.jpg|thumb|Woman with a '''thin''' waist]]

# Having little [[thickness]] or [[extent]] from one [[surface]] to its opposite.
#: {{ux|en|'''thin''' plate of metal;&nbsp; '''thin''' paper;&nbsp; '''thin''' board;&nbsp; '''thin''' covering}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1853|author=Charles MacFarlane|title=Kismet: or, The doom of Turkey|page=66
|passage=It was no mystery at all, or a mystery covered only with the '''thinnest''' and most transparent veil, that forced abortion is a common practice among Turkish women. The horrible secret as to the means and the drugs to be employed is pretty generally known, and where ignorance prevails there are "wise women," old hags, professional abortists, who go about the country relieving matrons of their burthens for a few piastres apiece {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Orwell Animal Farm|7
|passage=Out of spite, the human beings pretended not to believe that it was Snowball who had destroyed the windmill: they said that it had fallen down because the walls were too '''thin'''.}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Ashley Strickland|title=Scientists just created the world’s thinnest gold and it’s two atoms thick|url=https://www.cnn.com/2019/08/06/world/thinnest-gold-scn/index.html|date=2019-08-06|passage=The newest form of gold created in a lab is the thickness of two atoms, according to a new study. It’s only 0.47 nanometers thick, which is one million times '''thinner''' than a human finger nail. {{...}} This makes it the '''thinnest''' unsupported gold ever created and it could be used in electronics and medical devices going forward.<br>The gold is made up of two layers of atoms stacked on top of each other. But don’t let the thin structure fool you.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20200804181458/https://www.cnn.com/2019/08/06/world/thinnest-gold-scn/index.html}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Rishabh Sabarwal|title=Fortnite hitboxes: Do skins have a competitive advantage?|magazine=w:Dexerto|url=https://www.dexerto.com/fortnite/fortnite-hitboxes-do-skins-have-a-competitive-advantage-2222816/|date=2024-03-16|passage=However, the misconception regarding skin hitboxes was created by a subset of players who believed that wearing '''thinner''' skins enhanced their gameplay.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240805054700/https://www.dexerto.com/fortnite/fortnite-hitboxes-do-skins-have-a-competitive-advantage-2222816/}}
# Very [[narrow]] in all diameters; '''having''' a [[cross section]] that is small in all directions.
#: {{syn|en|twiggy}}
#: {{ux|en|'''thin''' wire; '''thin''' string}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=July 6, 2015|author=|title=Assessment of the Impact of Zoledronic Acid on Ovariectomized Osteoporosis Model Using Micro-CT Scanning|journal=PLOS ONE|url=http://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0132104|doi=10.1371/journal.pone.0132104|volume=|issue=|pages=
|passage=Typically, osteoporosis causes the amount of trabecular bone to be reduced and the bone to become '''thinner''', while the intertrabecular space enlarges and the interconnected structure of trabecular bone is disrupted.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220401091906/https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0132104}}
# Having little body fat or flesh; [[slim]]; [[slender]]; [[lean]]; [[gaunt]].
#: {{ux|en|'''thin''' person}}
# Of low [[viscosity]] or low [[specific gravity]].
#: {{ux|en|Water is '''thinner''' than honey.}}
# [[scarce|Scarce]]; not close, crowded, or numerous; not filling the space.
#: {{ux|en|The trees of a forest are '''thin'''; the corn or grass is '''thin'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Addison Italy
|passage=Ferrara is very large, but extremely '''thin''' of people.}}
# {{lb|en|golf}} Describing a poorly played [[golf]] shot where the ball is struck by the bottom part of the club head. See [[fat]], [[shank]], [[toe]].
# Lacking body or volume; small; feeble; not full.
#: {{ux|en|a '''thin''', tight-lipped smile}}
#* {{RQ:Dryden Don Sebastian
|passage='''thin''', hollow sounds, and lamentable screams}}
# Slight; small; slender; flimsy; superficial; inadequate; not sufficient for a covering.
#: {{ux|en|a '''thin''' disguise}}
# {{lb|en|aviation}} Of a route: relatively little used.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2016|author=Hartmut Wolf; Peter Forsyth; David Gillen|title=Liberalization in Aviation|page=105
|passage=In short, we previously found that '''thin''' routes benefit from an increase in competition in the Spanish airline market when considering routes that were monopoly routes in 2001.}}
# Poor; scanty; without money or success.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1945|author=Jack Henry|title=What Price Crime?|page=92
|passage=Like their friends the "draggers," the "hoisters" or shoplifters are having a '''thin''' time these days, {{...}}}}

